---
title: Shared Promotions
description: Let a whole community contribute to one goal and reward everyone who took part.
nav:
  title: Shared Goals
  path: Digital Assets/Loyalty Programs
  order: 2
---
A shared Promotion pools the progress of every member toward a single community goal. For example, once members have made 1,000 payments between them, everyone who contributed earns a reward.

Shared Promotions are challenges with a `shared` target. Each member still gets their own [Promotion Membership](/api/promotion-memberships), but qualifying Events move one shared tally that lives on the Promotion itself.

## The Shared Target

Set `params.target.type` to `shared` and `amount` to the community goal. Every qualifying Event adds 1 to the shared tally, regardless of who generated it.

```json {% title="1,000 payments unlock a reward" %}
{
  "type": "challenge",
  "eventType": "payment-request:paid",
  "params": {
    "target": {
      "type": "shared",
      "amount": "1000"
    },
    "rewards": {
      "and": [
        { "assetType": "centrapay.nzd.main", "amount": "500" }
      ]
    }
  }
}
```

The running total is exposed as `params.target.progress` on the [Promotion](/api/promotions#promotion-target-model). It starts at zero and never exceeds `amount` - once the goal is reached, further Events stop contributing.

A shared Promotion must not be given an `endsAt`. A community goal has to stay open until it is reached, so the only thing that ends the Promotion is reaching its target.

## Reaching the Goal

When the shared tally reaches `amount`, the Promotion ends by itself. Ending it finalises every membership under it:

- members who contributed at least once are completed, and their rewards are issued;
- members who never contributed expire without a reward.

## Tracking the Tally

[List Activities for Promotion](/api/promotions#list-activities-for-promotion) returns a paginated history of the Promotion. Shared Promotions record a `promotion:shared-progress-incremented` [activity](/api/promotions#promotion-activity-model) for every contribution, carrying the contributing `accountId` and the `targetProgress` at that moment.
